  "domain": "governance",
  "definition": "A policy framework is a structured set of principles, rules, standards, and processes established by a government body, standards organisation, or institution to guide decision-making, regulate behaviour, and ensure accountability within a defined domain. It translates high-level objectives \u2014 such as safety, fairness, or interoperability \u2014 into operational requirements and compliance mechanisms. Policy frameworks provide the normative scaffolding that enables coordinated action across organisations and jurisdictions.",
